# Subproject 2 — Design System & Layout Shell

## Context

This is a **Next.js 14+ (App Router) + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS + Framer Motion** personal portfolio project. **Subproject 1 is complete** — the repo already has a working `create-next-app` scaffold with TypeScript, App Router, Tailwind CSS, ESLint, Prettier, tsconfig path aliases (`@/components`, `@/lib`, `@/content`, etc.), and the base folder structure (`app/`, `components/`, `lib/`, `content/`, `public/`). `npm run build` passes cleanly.

Your job is **Subproject 2: Design System & Layout Shell**. After this subproject, the app must still compile and build cleanly (`npm run build`), and the browser should show a styled page with a working responsive navbar and footer.

---

## Deliverables

### 1. Tailwind Theme Config (Light/Dark Mode)

In `tailwind.config.ts`:

- **Colors**: Define a semantic color palette using CSS custom properties so light/dark mode works via a class toggle (`dark` class on `<html>`). At minimum define tokens for: `background`, `foreground`, `primary`, `primary-foreground`, `secondary`, `secondary-foreground`, `muted`, `muted-foreground`, `accent`, `accent-foreground`, `border`, `card`, `card-foreground`, `destructive`, `destructive-foreground`.
- **Fonts**: Configure two font families — a sans-serif for body text (Inter or Geist Sans) and a mono font for code/accents (JetBrains Mono or Geist Mono). Load them via `next/font/google` (or `next/font/local`) in the root layout and pass the CSS variable to Tailwind.
- **Spacing / Border Radius**: Add a `radius` design token (e.g., `--radius: 0.5rem`) referenced in Tailwind config for consistent rounded corners.
- **Dark mode strategy**: Use `darkMode: 'class'` in Tailwind config.

Create a `app/globals.css` that defines the CSS custom properties for both `:root` (light) and `.dark` (dark) selectors.

### 2. Theme Provider & Toggle

- Create `components/theme-provider.tsx` — a client component that wraps `next-themes` (`ThemeProvider` from `next-themes` package). Install `next-themes`.
- Create `components/theme-toggle.tsx` — a button that cycles between light/dark/system using `useTheme()` from `next-themes`. Use a sun/moon icon (inline SVG or `lucide-react`). Keep it accessible (`aria-label`, keyboard-operable).

### 3. Root Layout (`app/layout.tsx`)

- Import and apply the font variables.
- Wrap `{children}` in the `ThemeProvider` (attribute="class", defaultTheme="system", enableSystem).
- Set base `<html>` attributes: `lang="en"`, `suppressHydrationWarning`.
- Add baseline `metadata` export: site title, description, favicons (placeholder is fine).
- Apply global styles from `globals.css`.

### 4. Reusable UI Primitives

Create these in `components/ui/`. Each must be a well-typed, composable React component with `className` merging (use `clsx` + `tailwind-merge` — install both, create a `lib/utils.ts` exporting a `cn()` helper).

| Component | File | Key Props | Notes |
|-----------|------|-----------|-------|
| **Container** | `container.tsx` | `children`, `className` | Max-width wrapper (`max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8`) |
| **Section** | `section.tsx` | `children`, `id`, `className` | Full-width section with vertical padding, accepts `id` for anchor links |
| **Button** | `button.tsx` | `variant` (`primary`, `secondary`, `outline`, `ghost`), `size` (`sm`, `md`, `lg`), `asChild` | Styled `<button>` or renders as child element (link etc.) via a simple `asChild` pattern using `Slot` from `@radix-ui/react-slot` (install it). |
| **Badge** | `badge.tsx` | `variant` (`default`, `secondary`, `outline`), `children` | Small label/tag pill |
| **Card** | `card.tsx` | `children`, `className` | Card wrapper + subcomponents: `CardHeader`, `CardTitle`, `CardDescription`, `CardContent`, `CardFooter` |

### 5. Global Navbar

Create `components/navbar.tsx`:

- **Desktop**: Horizontal nav with logo/name on the left, nav links on the right (`Home`, `About`, `Projects`, `Blog`, `Contact`). Include the `ThemeToggle` button.
- **Mobile (< md breakpoint)**: Hamburger icon that opens a slide-in or dropdown mobile menu listing the same links. Animate open/close with Framer Motion. Clicking a link or clicking outside closes the menu.
- Links should use `next/link` and point to `/#about`, `/#projects`, `/blog`, `/#contact` etc. (hash links for same-page sections, real routes for blog).
- Navbar should be `sticky top-0` with a subtle backdrop blur and border-bottom.
- **Accessibility**: Use `<nav>` landmark, `aria-expanded` on mobile toggle, focus-trap is nice-to-have.

### 6. Footer

Create `components/footer.tsx`:

- Simple footer with: copyright line (`© {currentYear} <Name>. All rights reserved.`), social links row (GitHub, LinkedIn, Twitter/X, Email — use placeholder `#` hrefs), and optional "Built with Next.js & Tailwind" tagline.
- Style: muted text, centered or flex layout, top border separator.

### 7. Compose in Root Layout

Wire everything together in `app/layout.tsx` so the page structure is:

```
<ThemeProvider>
  <Navbar />
  <main>{children}</main>
  <Footer />
</ThemeProvider>
```

Update `app/page.tsx` to render a placeholder hero section that uses `Container`, `Section`, and `Button` so you can visually verify the design system in the browser.

